// Title: BPFtrace Unsafe Option Usage
// Sigma ID: f8341cb2-ee25-43fa-a975-d8a5a9714b39
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Andreas Hunkeler (@Karneades)
// Date: 2022-02-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.004
// Description: Detects the usage of the unsafe bpftrace option
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of the unsafe option
// References:
//   - https://embracethered.com/blog/posts/2021/offensive-bpf-bpftrace/
//   - https://bpftrace.org/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_bpftrace_unsafe_option_usage.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "bpftrace" and ProcessCommandLine contains "--unsafe"
